WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:28.363
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:28.633 --> 00:30.051
TAKE CHARGE OF MY HEART

3
00:31.594 --> 00:32.762
Ms. Na Bo-bae.

4
00:34.806 --> 00:35.640
Yes?

5
00:36.558 --> 00:37.767
Me too.

6
00:39.727 --> 00:40.812
What do you mean?

7
00:41.938 --> 00:43.064
When I'm

8
00:43.773 --> 00:45.900
with you,

9
00:46.484 --> 00:48.862
I worry about you all the time.

10
00:49.445 --> 00:50.905
My heart's racing so fast…

11
00:55.118 --> 00:56.703
it feels like it will explode.

12
00:59.038 --> 01:00.290
Ms. Na.

13
01:01.958 --> 01:02.792
I…

14
01:06.129 --> 01:08.381
don't want to die before my heart surgery.

15
01:10.717 --> 01:11.551
Sorry?

16
01:11.634 --> 01:13.052
So…

17
01:15.054 --> 01:19.350
just stay within what I've planned and anticipated.

18
01:23.479 --> 01:25.315
I'll go out first.

19
01:25.815 --> 01:28.568
Don't let anyone see you come out.

20
01:35.283 --> 01:36.117
Oh, right.

21
01:37.202 --> 01:39.829
Text me every 30 minutes when you're with your friends.

22
01:42.081 --> 01:44.000
Ugh, I feel dizzy.

23
02:04.604 --> 02:05.855
Oh wow.

24
02:06.606 --> 02:09.359
I thought he was gonna confess or something.

25
02:10.276 --> 02:12.946
Then again, there's no way that jerk would do that.

26
02:16.908 --> 02:20.036
Our final concept is "A Night's Confession."

27
02:20.119 --> 02:20.954
For this one,

28
02:21.037 --> 02:25.458
the story follows two longtime friends who spend a night together at the resort.

29
02:25.541 --> 02:30.129
Naturally, they end up confessing their hidden feelings for each other.

30
02:30.213 --> 02:31.589
That's all.

31
02:37.553 --> 02:38.638
What do you think?

32
02:38.721 --> 02:41.516
We put it together in script format, like you suggested.

33
02:41.599 --> 02:44.102
-Ms. Na, which do you like best? -Me?

34
02:45.311 --> 02:46.854
I think

35
02:46.938 --> 02:50.692
the third concept would be the easiest to dramatize.

36
02:52.277 --> 02:53.611
How so?

37
02:53.695 --> 02:56.197
The way they end up in the resort garden.

38
02:57.073 --> 02:59.701
Instead of following a past lover's trail,

39
02:59.784 --> 03:01.536
what if we made it an adventure?

40
03:02.954 --> 03:04.038
That could work.

41
03:04.122 --> 03:08.293
Mr. Ji falls into the mysterious world of TS Resort

42
03:08.376 --> 03:10.461
and embarks on an adventure there.

43
03:11.045 --> 03:14.048
As long as the protagonist's motivation is clear from the start,

44
03:14.132 --> 03:16.259
viewers can immediately connect with them.

45
03:16.884 --> 03:18.845
The motivation doesn't have to be deep.

46
03:18.928 --> 03:24.309
I think just a small sense of yearning or a simple desire is enough

47
03:24.392 --> 03:28.271
to carry the protagonist through the story.

48
03:28.354 --> 03:31.774
And since it's only about a minute long…

49
03:37.655 --> 03:39.449
If we build a narrative like this,

50
03:39.532 --> 03:41.492
it promotes TS Resort,

51
03:42.285 --> 03:43.828
gives us a bit of drama,

52
03:44.412 --> 03:47.623
and will be more fun for Mr. Ji to act in… I think.

53
03:51.502 --> 03:53.713
I like it. It sounds fun.

54
03:58.092 --> 04:00.136
You nailed the concept. Let's give her a hand.

55
04:00.219 --> 04:01.679
That's it!

56
04:38.424 --> 04:39.467
Door unlocked.

57
04:39.550 --> 04:40.802
Ms. Na Bo-bae.

58
04:40.885 --> 04:41.844
Yes?

59
04:42.345 --> 04:43.596
Today…

60
04:48.810 --> 04:49.644
You did well.

61
04:50.728 --> 04:53.940
Thanks to you, we were able to finalize the concept.

62
04:54.690 --> 04:58.069
Before we leave for Jeju island, I'm counting on you

63
04:59.570 --> 05:00.780
to write a great script.

64
05:03.032 --> 05:04.200
Jeez.

65
05:04.951 --> 05:06.994
Did you think my writing debut was a fluke?

66
05:07.078 --> 05:09.247
A minute-long script? I can do it in ten minutes.

67
05:09.330 --> 05:11.624
-You're getting carried away again. -I'm not.

68
05:11.707 --> 05:14.210
Okay, maybe ten minutes is a stretch.

69
05:15.044 --> 05:18.464
Give me an hour, and I'll write you a killer script.

70
05:18.548 --> 05:19.465
You'll see.

71
05:21.926 --> 05:23.094
Move over!

72
05:31.352 --> 05:33.062
Seriously…

73
05:46.951 --> 05:48.411
Wow.

74
05:49.203 --> 05:52.623
He thought something happened to Na Bo-bae and rushed over.

75
05:52.707 --> 05:54.459
Drove like he was racing.

76
05:55.209 --> 05:57.336
Freaking out, white as a ghost.

77
05:58.463 --> 06:01.883
Baek Ho-rang is serious about Na Bo-bae.

78
06:28.493 --> 06:29.327
Huh?

79
06:30.661 --> 06:31.746
What's wrong with me?

80
07:12.036 --> 07:12.870
Mr. Baek?

81
07:29.762 --> 07:31.430
Did you have something to say?

82
07:31.514 --> 07:32.765
"Something to say"?

83
07:33.724 --> 07:36.018
Do I look like I have nothing better to do?

84
07:37.186 --> 07:38.312
Don't mind me.

85
07:40.106 --> 07:41.482
Just do your job.

86
07:42.066 --> 07:43.442
What did I…

87
07:51.784 --> 07:52.994
Thank you.

88
07:54.579 --> 07:55.621
Ms. Na.

89
07:55.705 --> 07:57.623
I love the concept.

90
07:57.707 --> 07:58.541
Yes!

91
07:58.624 --> 08:02.003
Things he can experience on his adventure at the resort…

92
08:02.503 --> 08:03.504
Sounds great.

93
08:23.441 --> 08:25.192
Jeez, what's wrong with this?

94
08:29.196 --> 08:30.573
All right. Back to work.

95
08:31.782 --> 08:33.659
Sir?

96
08:33.743 --> 08:34.827
Sir!

97
08:36.412 --> 08:37.246
What was that?

98
08:38.539 --> 08:40.041
Did I do something wrong?

99
08:50.217 --> 08:51.677
Is there something down there?

100
08:56.599 --> 08:57.767
The other day,

101
08:57.850 --> 08:59.935
Ms. Na and I were under the desk…

102
09:00.686 --> 09:02.188
What? When did you get here?

103
09:02.271 --> 09:03.856
I've been here for a while.

104
09:05.650 --> 09:08.444
Never mind. Just spray some of that aroma spray.

105
09:10.404 --> 09:11.238
Yes, sir.

106
09:12.073 --> 09:13.157
By the way, sir.

107
09:14.784 --> 09:17.787
You seem to be getting a little too involved with Ms. Na.

108
09:18.287 --> 09:19.955
I suggest you keep your distance.

109
09:21.248 --> 09:23.709
Should I just send everyone on vacation?

110
09:23.793 --> 09:24.627
Sorry?

111
09:24.710 --> 09:27.380
I could send everyone on vacation and charge at home…

112
09:30.925 --> 09:31.801
I mean…

113
09:32.843 --> 09:36.222
It'd be nice to take some time to recharge.

114
09:36.305 --> 09:37.973
That's what I meant.

115
09:38.057 --> 09:38.891
Sir.

116
09:39.600 --> 09:42.311
We have a business trip to Jeju tomorrow.

117
09:44.480 --> 09:45.690
Ms. Na just texted.

118
09:47.066 --> 09:48.109
Did you hear me?

119
09:48.192 --> 09:50.403
Why did she text me out of the blue?

120
09:50.486 --> 09:53.072
Mr. Baek Ho-rang! I'm heading out first today.

121
09:53.155 --> 09:55.908
It's my sister's birthday, so I'm throwing her a party.

122
09:55.991 --> 09:57.576
I'll come home tonight.

123
10:04.458 --> 10:05.501
Damn it.

124
10:07.044 --> 10:08.045
Sir!

125
10:10.548 --> 10:11.632
Sir!

126
10:11.716 --> 10:12.591
Well…

127
10:13.384 --> 10:14.844
Did Ms. Na already leave?

128
10:14.927 --> 10:17.555
Yes, she said she had plans and left right away.

129
10:17.638 --> 10:19.432
Did you need her for something?

130
10:19.515 --> 10:20.891
What? No.

131
10:21.892 --> 10:24.186
Call it a day. See you at the airport tomorrow.

132
10:24.270 --> 10:25.187
-Yes, sir. -Yes, sir.

133
10:25.271 --> 10:26.272
Take care, sir.

134
10:26.355 --> 10:27.398
See you tomorrow.

135
10:33.362 --> 10:34.488
Sir.

136
10:36.031 --> 10:37.199
Hey.

137
10:39.410 --> 10:41.495
Our little sister is here!

138
10:42.037 --> 10:43.789
HAPPY BIRTHDAY!

139
10:44.582 --> 10:47.376
Why does he always make such a fuss?

140
10:47.460 --> 10:49.712
You hungry? What should we order for dinner?

141
10:50.296 --> 10:51.589
Order whatever you want.

142
10:51.672 --> 10:53.799
I got us lots of beer!

143
10:53.883 --> 10:55.384
Ta-da!

144
10:55.468 --> 10:58.053
It's Ji-hye's birthday. She should get to choose.

145
10:58.137 --> 10:58.971
That's right.

146
10:59.054 --> 11:00.055
It's my birthday,

147
11:00.139 --> 11:03.058
so the writer with the new Gangnam studio should treat us.

148
11:04.602 --> 11:06.604
Of course! What do you want to eat?

149
11:06.687 --> 11:08.314
-What should we order? -Chicken!

150
11:08.397 --> 11:10.316
-Fried chicken! -Chicken?

151
11:39.136 --> 11:41.555
I'm so full.

152
11:42.223 --> 11:43.057
Na Bo-bae!

153
11:43.140 --> 11:45.893
It sure is nice to have a successful little sister.

154
11:45.976 --> 11:47.520
Successful? Please.

155
11:48.103 --> 11:49.522
My show isn't even out yet.

156
11:50.397 --> 11:51.440
When your show's out,

157
11:51.524 --> 11:53.692
fried chicken and tteokbokki won't cut it.

158
11:53.776 --> 11:55.236
We'll have to get some premium Korean beef.

159
11:55.736 --> 11:56.987
Your show…

160
11:57.488 --> 11:58.906
When's it coming out?

161
12:00.324 --> 12:02.326
Well, I'm not sure.

162
12:02.952 --> 12:06.539
Shows take at least a few years to come out,

163
12:06.622 --> 12:09.124
so it'll probably be a while.

164
12:09.208 --> 12:13.045
We've already waited three years. Now we have to wait even longer?

165
12:13.128 --> 12:15.130
Well, maybe another year…

166
12:15.214 --> 12:16.590
Or two?

167
12:20.719 --> 12:22.388
Something's fishy.

168
12:23.639 --> 12:24.974
Is it really going well?

169
12:27.393 --> 12:28.644
Of course!

170
12:28.727 --> 12:33.107
I've been doing a ton of research, and my script's coming along well.

171
12:33.190 --> 12:35.609
My romance scenes are so much better now. And…

172
12:38.112 --> 12:39.113
When I'm

173
12:39.613 --> 12:42.074
with you,

174
12:43.242 --> 12:45.452
I worry about you every day.

175
12:46.161 --> 12:47.663
My heart's racing so fast…

176
12:48.956 --> 12:50.541
it feels like it will explode.

177
12:52.668 --> 12:53.919
And what?

178
12:54.003 --> 12:56.463
What were you thinking about? You totally spaced out.

179
12:56.547 --> 12:57.673
Huh?

180
12:57.756 --> 12:58.924
What?

181
12:59.008 --> 13:00.885
-What? I did not. -Huh?

182
13:00.968 --> 13:03.429
She's acting really weird. What's going on?

183
13:04.013 --> 13:05.014
I know, right?

184
13:05.681 --> 13:08.475
That's the look

185
13:09.685 --> 13:12.479
Na Ji-hye gets when she thinks about her fiancé.

186
13:12.563 --> 13:14.231
What are you talking about?

187
13:14.315 --> 13:15.816
Fiancé?

188
13:18.485 --> 13:19.820
You two are hilarious.

189
13:19.904 --> 13:22.907
How could you say that when I've been working so hard?

190
13:25.492 --> 13:28.162
Ji-hye, something's definitely up with her.

191
13:28.245 --> 13:29.663
I can feel it.

192
13:33.709 --> 13:35.169
You seeing someone?

193
13:35.252 --> 13:37.379
Seeing someone? I have to write my script!

194
13:37.463 --> 13:38.714
Also…

195
13:39.757 --> 13:42.384
Did you forget about my electric powers?

196
13:42.468 --> 13:43.552
I'm leaving.

197
13:43.636 --> 13:45.429
-Huh? -Where do you think you're going?

198
13:48.390 --> 13:49.600
You should stay the night.

199
13:50.768 --> 13:53.646
You're acting really suspicious. Trying to run away?

200
13:53.729 --> 13:56.148
Where are you going? Don't make me use tae kwon do on you!

201
13:56.231 --> 13:59.109
I… Then I'll use my electric powers!

202
14:15.292 --> 14:17.336
When is she coming home?

203
14:23.676 --> 14:24.802
PORTABLE CHARGER

204
14:27.429 --> 14:28.263
Hello?

205
14:29.181 --> 14:33.018
Oh, Mr. Baek. I'm sorry, I don't think I can come home today.

206
14:33.102 --> 14:35.437
Why not? You said you'd be back tonight.

207
14:35.521 --> 14:38.482
My sister and brother insist that I stay the night.

208
14:39.066 --> 14:42.069
I said I have a work trip tomorrow, but they said I should leave from here

209
14:42.152 --> 14:44.446
since it's closer to the airport and I have all my stuff.

210
14:44.530 --> 14:46.699
What do we do about charging you?

211
14:46.782 --> 14:48.784
Should I sneak out at dawn?

212
14:50.327 --> 14:54.289
I've got enough charge to last about 20 hours, even if we're apart.

213
14:55.040 --> 14:57.710
You can supercharge me at the airport tomorrow.

214
14:58.585 --> 15:00.796
Don't worry. Stay the night.

215
15:00.879 --> 15:01.964
But still--

216
15:02.047 --> 15:03.507
I said it's fine.

217
15:03.590 --> 15:05.342
You'll be busy tomorrow.

218
15:05.426 --> 15:08.387
Take this opportunity to relax with your family.

219
15:08.887 --> 15:11.140
Thank you. See you tomorrow.

220
15:30.701 --> 15:31.785
What's wrong with me?

221
15:32.286 --> 15:34.705
Baek Ho-rang, are you crazy?

222
15:50.429 --> 15:51.513
Oh!

223
15:52.014 --> 15:54.391
I said I'd redecorate the garage for her.

224
15:55.809 --> 15:56.643
That's right.

225
15:57.144 --> 15:59.063
That's why I kept thinking about her.

226
15:59.146 --> 16:00.481
So that's what it was.

227
16:04.151 --> 16:06.070
Hey, Mr. Yoon. It's me.

228
16:06.153 --> 16:08.739
Find me an interior designer. The best one.

229
16:08.822 --> 16:10.199
Sir? Right now?

230
16:10.282 --> 16:11.533
Yeah, right now.

231
16:12.117 --> 16:14.828
-Mr. Yoon, ever heard of flexing? -Sorry?

232
16:14.912 --> 16:17.873
I want a top-of-the-line interior. A real chaebol flex.

233
16:17.956 --> 16:18.832
Got it?

234
16:18.916 --> 16:21.543
I don't know what has you so worried at this hour, but--

235
16:21.627 --> 16:23.170
No, listen.

236
16:23.253 --> 16:24.505
I really need it.

237
16:24.588 --> 16:26.840
And send over a cake

238
16:27.466 --> 16:30.260
and the finest Korean beef right now.

239
16:30.803 --> 16:31.637
Yeah.

240
16:41.814 --> 16:44.149
Will his battery really last the night?

241
16:45.901 --> 16:47.444
RUBBER GLOVE

242
16:47.528 --> 16:49.988
MR. BAEK HO-R

243
16:50.072 --> 16:51.907
Never mind.

244
16:52.407 --> 16:53.575
Forget it.

245
16:58.997 --> 17:01.083
JOSEE, THE TIGER AND THE FISH

246
17:03.544 --> 17:08.382
HO-RANG

247
17:10.425 --> 17:12.010
Why can't I focus?

248
17:12.594 --> 17:14.346
Come on. Focus.

249
17:18.559 --> 17:24.064
I-HYEOK AND HYE-JU WALK THROUGH THE HAUNTED HOUSE

250
17:24.148 --> 17:25.357
I'm a little scared.

251
17:25.440 --> 17:26.733
(FEARFULLY)

252
17:26.817 --> 17:28.318
Can we just get out of here?

253
17:30.362 --> 17:31.363
Ma'am.

254
17:31.446 --> 17:32.281
(FINDING HER CUTE)

255
17:32.364 --> 17:33.740
I didn't expect you to be this scared.

256
17:34.575 --> 17:35.576
You're not scared?

257
17:35.659 --> 17:36.660
(DEFENSIVELY)

258
17:36.743 --> 17:38.412
I hate jump scares and--

259
17:38.495 --> 17:40.789
(THROWING HERSELF INTO HIS ARMS)

260
17:43.250 --> 17:44.668
I'm scared.

261
17:49.006 --> 17:50.674
I-HYEOK HOLDS HYE-JU'S HAND

262
17:50.757 --> 17:52.134
Ma'am.

263
17:52.217 --> 17:53.427
Run.

264
17:56.346 --> 17:58.974
I-HYEOK RUNS, HOLDING HYE-JU'S HAND TIGHT

265
18:02.019 --> 18:05.522
NOTHING SCARES HYE-JU AND I-HYEOK ANYMORE

266
18:15.240 --> 18:16.200
That's more like it.

267
18:16.283 --> 18:19.161
Yeah, the male lead should be holding the female lead's hand.

268
18:19.244 --> 18:22.915
Running with the ghost? Makes no sense.

269
18:24.917 --> 18:27.920
Baek Ho-rang. He's hilarious.

270
18:32.799 --> 18:36.762
That's the look Na Ji-hye gets when she thinks about her fiancé.

271
18:36.845 --> 18:37.763
You seeing someone?

272
18:38.764 --> 18:40.557
Hilarious? Not at all.

273
18:41.141 --> 18:42.768
Seeing someone? Yeah, right.

274
18:43.268 --> 18:45.979
It's an act of compassion.

275
18:46.063 --> 18:47.189
I'm saving a life.

276
18:47.272 --> 18:49.524
Besides, Mr. Baek has Ms. Han.

277
18:54.696 --> 18:57.491
And since it's an act of compassion,

278
18:59.243 --> 19:05.082
it should be okay to call and ask how much battery he has left.

279
19:08.710 --> 19:09.711
No!

280
19:10.504 --> 19:11.546
No.

281
19:12.256 --> 19:13.215
No.

282
19:13.715 --> 19:15.425
Get a grip.

283
19:30.607 --> 19:32.776
Mr. Baek, what are you doing here?

284
19:33.652 --> 19:36.363
Well, I…

285
19:36.446 --> 19:37.864
It's your sister's birthday.

286
19:37.948 --> 19:40.284
I thought it'd be rude to not acknowledge it,

287
19:41.702 --> 19:44.746
since you help charge my battery and all.

288
19:45.497 --> 19:46.498
And I realized

289
19:47.124 --> 19:50.085
you wished me a happy birthday too, so…

290
19:51.336 --> 19:52.212
But…

291
19:53.463 --> 19:56.925
So you bought all that and ran all the way here at this hour?

292
19:57.009 --> 19:58.760
I didn't run. I drove here.

293
19:58.844 --> 20:01.179
And Mr. Yoon bought these.

294
20:01.680 --> 20:02.848
Don't get the wrong idea.

295
20:02.931 --> 20:06.685
TS Resort takes employee welfare seriously.

296
20:06.768 --> 20:07.769
But…

297
20:08.729 --> 20:10.564
Employee welfare? At this hour?

298
20:10.647 --> 20:11.982
Take it. Come on.

299
20:16.528 --> 20:19.614
What? You're just leaving? What about your charge?

300
20:20.198 --> 20:21.325
Huh? Charge?

301
20:21.825 --> 20:25.203
Well, I'm at 85% now.

302
20:25.287 --> 20:27.706
If I lose 4% an hour,

303
20:27.789 --> 20:31.084
I'll still have 50% if we meet by 6 a.m.

304
20:31.585 --> 20:33.670
So there's no need to worry.

305
20:33.754 --> 20:35.088
But still--

306
20:35.172 --> 20:37.466
And I'm not that weak.

307
20:50.771 --> 20:52.898
Close the window before bed. See you tomorrow.

308
20:52.981 --> 20:54.483
But Mr. Baek…

309
20:58.236 --> 20:59.279
What…

310
21:27.724 --> 21:30.936
It's bad for my heart if it gets too high.

311
21:32.396 --> 21:33.730
Calm down.

312
21:47.828 --> 21:49.162
Stop it.

313
22:27.159 --> 22:29.703
Was he thinking about me

314
22:30.620 --> 22:31.621
the whole time?

315
22:38.462 --> 22:39.421
What am I saying?

316
22:40.297 --> 22:41.381
Get a grip, Na Bo-bae.

317
22:41.965 --> 22:42.883
Get a grip.

318
23:03.236 --> 23:04.488
Ms. Na Bo-bae!

319
23:05.489 --> 23:06.865
Mr. Baek Ho-rang!

320
23:22.214 --> 23:23.757
Oh, to be young again.

321
23:23.840 --> 23:26.968
Looks like one of them's been abroad for a few years.

322
23:33.558 --> 23:35.435
I need a charge.

323
23:35.519 --> 23:36.770
Yeah.

324
23:36.853 --> 23:39.397
I was up all night working.

325
23:39.481 --> 23:42.442
That must be why my battery's draining faster than usual.

326
23:43.568 --> 23:46.154
-I'm worried about my heart. -So you were up all night.

327
23:46.238 --> 23:47.072
Yes.

328
23:47.155 --> 23:48.907
I rushed over because of your battery.

329
23:48.990 --> 23:51.451
Really, that was the only reason.

330
23:52.786 --> 23:53.912
Thank you

331
23:53.995 --> 23:56.414
for caring about my life.

332
23:56.498 --> 23:58.792
It's just an act of compassion.

333
23:58.875 --> 24:00.544
Oh, an act of compassion?

334
24:05.048 --> 24:07.050
Supercharging here is too risky.

335
24:07.133 --> 24:08.760
Let's go to the VIP lounge.

336
24:09.344 --> 24:10.387
Let's go. Quickly.

337
24:18.228 --> 24:19.521
Mr. Baek.

338
24:20.272 --> 24:21.106
You're early.

339
24:22.232 --> 24:23.066
Oh, yes.

340
24:24.734 --> 24:25.569
Yes.

341
24:26.820 --> 24:29.030
You're here early too, Ms. Han.

342
24:29.698 --> 24:31.616
Three hours early.

343
24:32.367 --> 24:35.412
I figured you'd get here three or four hours early.

344
24:37.872 --> 24:38.707
Have a seat.

345
24:39.207 --> 24:40.917
Let's grab a quick breakfast.

346
24:43.044 --> 24:44.713
Sure. Let's do that.

347
24:45.714 --> 24:47.090
Hold on.

348
24:47.674 --> 24:51.720
I have to get something from Mr. Yoon.

349
24:51.803 --> 24:52.637
Excuse me.

350
24:54.180 --> 24:55.056
Sure. Go ahead.

351
24:55.890 --> 24:56.725
All right.

352
25:07.986 --> 25:10.030
I don't think we can do it in the lounge.

353
25:10.739 --> 25:13.116
Let's just do it here. Nobody's around.

354
25:13.199 --> 25:14.993
First, put your sunglasses on.

355
25:20.790 --> 25:22.626
No, I'm serious.

356
25:24.586 --> 25:25.920
-No. Not this way. -Shoot.

357
25:26.421 --> 25:27.255
Wait up!

358
25:27.339 --> 25:30.091
You know you have to take off your shoes on the plane, right?

359
25:30.175 --> 25:31.509
Seriously, Ms. Yang?

360
25:31.593 --> 25:33.720
Even schoolkids don't fall for that anymore.

361
25:33.803 --> 25:34.971
But it's true.

362
25:35.722 --> 25:37.390
Are we going on vacation?

363
25:37.474 --> 25:39.517
What's with the outfit, Mr. Lee?

364
25:39.601 --> 25:42.437
I dressed up a little. I'll change when we get there.

365
25:42.520 --> 25:43.396
Seriously.

366
25:43.480 --> 25:45.857
Ms. Na said she'd come separately.

367
25:45.940 --> 25:46.900
Isn't she here yet?

368
25:46.983 --> 25:49.944
Why would she come separately? She's probably with Mr. Baek.

369
25:54.699 --> 25:57.243
Damn it, they keep popping up. What do we do?

370
25:57.327 --> 25:59.871
At this rate, I can't charge you. What's your battery at?

371
26:01.581 --> 26:03.792
Right now, it's at 35%.

372
26:03.875 --> 26:04.918
Thirty-five?

373
26:08.880 --> 26:09.881
Follow me.

374
26:13.968 --> 26:16.346
You're eating breakfast at a time like this?

375
26:16.429 --> 26:19.224
No one from the company will come here.

376
26:19.307 --> 26:22.060
It's a good hiding spot. Staying close won't look suspicious.

377
26:22.143 --> 26:23.770
Don't sit there. Sit next to me.

378
26:23.853 --> 26:24.729
Oh.

379
26:35.657 --> 26:38.993
Your jeyuk and doenjang-jjigae.

380
26:39.077 --> 26:40.412
Enjoy your meal.

381
26:40.495 --> 26:42.122
-Thank you. -Thank you.

382
26:46.126 --> 26:47.168
Let's…

383
26:47.252 --> 26:49.254
Let's eat while we…

384
26:49.337 --> 26:50.505
-Just come. -Sure.

385
26:50.588 --> 26:52.632
-You talk too much. -Your luggage…

386
26:52.716 --> 26:54.426
-Wait, Director. -Stop whining.

387
26:54.509 --> 26:55.844
Just come.

388
26:55.927 --> 26:57.846
-Follow me. -Why do you have so much luggage?

389
26:57.929 --> 27:00.098
-Be careful with them. -They're heavy.

390
27:00.181 --> 27:02.976
You gotta hit a Korean restaurant at the airport.

391
27:03.768 --> 27:06.813
Why eat Korean food when we're going to Jeju?

392
27:06.896 --> 27:09.607
It's just my little pre-flight ritual.

393
27:09.691 --> 27:11.693
Just eat. Enough complaining.

394
27:20.535 --> 27:21.870
Huh?

395
27:22.996 --> 27:24.372
-What's that? -What?

396
27:26.458 --> 27:27.542
Say what?

397
27:33.673 --> 27:35.633
What are they eating? It must be good.

398
27:35.717 --> 27:37.177
Their faces are buried in the bowl.

399
27:37.260 --> 27:38.178
-Seo-jeong. -Yes?

400
27:38.261 --> 27:39.137
Let's have that.

401
27:39.220 --> 27:40.221
Sure.

402
27:40.305 --> 27:42.056
They could've sat across from each other.

403
27:42.140 --> 27:45.018
Couples can be so over the top, you know.

404
27:45.727 --> 27:46.603
So over the top.

405
27:47.103 --> 27:48.146
I'm divorced, you know.

406
27:49.522 --> 27:51.858
Okay, I'll go order. The company card, please.

407
27:52.442 --> 27:54.152
Can't you just go?

408
27:54.235 --> 27:56.404
-Company card! -I don't have it. You pay.

409
27:56.488 --> 27:59.199
-We'll split it. -Split it? I'll split your head open.

410
28:00.074 --> 28:01.868
-You want everything free. -What's that?

411
28:01.951 --> 28:03.745
Doenjang-jjigae. Bibimbap.

412
28:04.245 --> 28:06.164
-Where do I order Korean food? -Chopsticks…

413
28:06.664 --> 28:07.624
Where are they?

414
28:18.843 --> 28:21.387
Excuse me. Where are the chopsticks and spoons?

415
28:23.681 --> 28:25.391
What's your battery at now?

416
28:25.475 --> 28:26.768
It's at 41%.

417
28:26.851 --> 28:28.478
It's still risky.

418
28:31.689 --> 28:35.151
I think we should finish charging on the plane.

419
28:51.668 --> 28:53.586
Mr. Yoon. Ms. Na Bo-bae…

420
28:54.254 --> 28:56.422
I mean, the secretaries. Where are they?

421
28:56.506 --> 29:00.009
I think there was a mix-up with the reservation.

422
29:00.093 --> 29:03.221
The other secretaries and staff are in economy.

423
29:04.097 --> 29:06.766
Oh. Economy?

424
29:06.850 --> 29:10.645
Economy's over ten meters away.

425
29:28.746 --> 29:31.875
What took so long? We said we'd meet after the seatbelt sign.

426
29:31.958 --> 29:33.376
I've got too many eyes on me.

427
29:34.836 --> 29:37.255
Let's hug and get it over with before anyone comes.

428
29:38.131 --> 29:39.757
Is the passenger check complete?

429
29:39.841 --> 29:41.050
-Yes, it's done. -What the…

430
29:41.134 --> 29:43.386
-Let's get the drink cart ready. -Okay.

431
29:53.730 --> 29:56.190
I'll get the cups. You get the drinks.

432
29:56.274 --> 29:57.275
Sure.

433
29:59.903 --> 30:03.781
Please prepare the sodas and other drinks. And the coffee too.

434
30:24.969 --> 30:27.430
What is it? Did we land?

435
30:29.891 --> 30:31.851
Please fasten your seat belt.

436
30:33.978 --> 30:35.855
Seat belt. Ms. Go, your seat belt.

437
30:35.939 --> 30:38.316
-Please fasten your seat belt. -What? Are we there?

438
30:39.442 --> 30:41.653
Please be seated and fasten your seat belt.

439
30:41.736 --> 30:42.987
What happened?

440
30:43.571 --> 30:45.281
-I'm sorry. -Don't do that!

441
30:45.365 --> 30:46.950
The plane shook again.

442
30:59.420 --> 31:02.507
I'm sorry. I thought I was going to fall.

443
31:02.590 --> 31:03.967
Did I startle you?

444
31:04.050 --> 31:06.719
No. Not at all.

445
31:07.720 --> 31:09.806
It's the turbulence.

446
31:09.889 --> 31:13.351
This airline has an A safety rating for domestic flights.

447
31:13.434 --> 31:15.853
Very low accident rate. That's why I chose it.

448
31:15.937 --> 31:17.438
Why's this thing beeping?

449
31:17.522 --> 31:19.774
You weren't startled, so why's your heart rate…

450
31:21.651 --> 31:22.527
Could it be…

451
31:22.610 --> 31:23.987
I was just startled!

452
31:24.070 --> 31:25.446
Don't get the wrong idea.

453
31:26.489 --> 31:27.573
I was just startled.

454
31:27.657 --> 31:29.200
I didn't say anything.

455
31:30.660 --> 31:31.953
Are you all right?

456
31:32.453 --> 31:34.455
We're experiencing turbulence.

457
31:34.539 --> 31:37.667
Please return to your seat until it subsides.

458
31:39.293 --> 31:41.254
My stomach's acting up.

459
31:41.337 --> 31:43.923
I'm kind of in the middle of it. I can't really stop.

460
31:44.716 --> 31:46.676
I'll just stay seated here.

461
31:48.469 --> 31:50.179
All right.

462
31:56.519 --> 31:57.603
Ms. Na.

463
31:59.105 --> 32:00.273
You can't stop?

464
32:00.356 --> 32:03.359
Oh, be quiet.

465
32:07.739 --> 32:10.033
We'll charge again later if we get a chance.

466
32:10.700 --> 32:12.952
I think it's okay now, so I'll head out first.

467
32:13.036 --> 32:14.328
Come out in a bit.

468
32:16.039 --> 32:18.166
Stop laughing!

469
32:35.475 --> 32:37.226
It's so hot in here.

470
32:48.446 --> 32:50.448
-Nice, right? -Yes, very.

471
32:58.623 --> 33:00.041
It's been a while, Mr. Heo.

472
33:00.124 --> 33:02.460
It's an honor to have you here in Jeju, sir.

473
33:02.543 --> 33:04.170
The honor's all mine.

474
33:04.253 --> 33:06.255
You run this place so well.

475
33:06.339 --> 33:08.591
Our Seoul resort has a lot to live up to.

476
33:08.674 --> 33:10.134
Not at all.

477
33:10.218 --> 33:11.844
The filming locations are all set,

478
33:11.928 --> 33:14.305
and the actor's already here.

479
33:14.388 --> 33:15.681
-Is that so? -Yes.

480
33:18.684 --> 33:20.603
-Hello. -Hello.

481
33:21.687 --> 33:22.730
Hello.

482
33:23.773 --> 33:25.942
-Looking good as always. -You're too kind.

483
33:29.695 --> 33:30.571
Have you eaten?

484
33:30.655 --> 33:32.281
Yeah. You?

485
33:37.662 --> 33:41.207
I heard you weren't arriving until this afternoon.

486
33:41.707 --> 33:45.920
I wanted to check out the set, so I shuffled my schedule and came early.

487
33:49.882 --> 33:52.552
Awesome! This room's really nice too.

488
33:53.052 --> 33:55.638
This is insane. The view's incredible.

489
33:57.557 --> 33:59.517
I need a photo of this.

490
34:00.852 --> 34:04.272
Wow, I think the rooms here are better than ours.

491
34:05.982 --> 34:08.651
Ms. Go, which room are you staying in?

492
34:08.734 --> 34:09.735
Let me see.

493
34:10.903 --> 34:12.113
Wow.

494
34:15.867 --> 34:16.951
Ms. Na.

495
34:19.745 --> 34:20.580
Yes?

496
34:23.958 --> 34:25.710
Mr. Baek is asking for you.

497
34:43.686 --> 34:45.771
Mr. Yoon, why are you here?

498
34:47.607 --> 34:49.650
Am I not allowed to be here?

499
34:50.234 --> 34:53.196
You're just charging.

500
34:58.534 --> 35:00.203
No. Get out.

501
35:02.246 --> 35:03.122
Huh?

502
35:03.206 --> 35:04.540
Get out.

503
35:06.542 --> 35:07.627
Huh?

504
35:07.710 --> 35:08.669
You're not leaving?

505
35:10.213 --> 35:11.422
Well…

506
35:11.505 --> 35:13.633
I mean, wouldn't it be okay

507
35:14.133 --> 35:15.301
for him to stay?

508
35:15.384 --> 35:17.178
We're just charging. No big deal.

509
35:17.261 --> 35:18.846
You said it's an act of compassion.

510
35:18.930 --> 35:22.225
If we're charging in the name of such a noble cause,

511
35:22.725 --> 35:25.186
shouldn't we keep it private and sacred?

512
35:27.313 --> 35:28.356
But…

513
35:28.439 --> 35:31.484
-I mean, he already knows everything-- -I'm very sensitive.

514
35:31.567 --> 35:33.903
I get distracted when there's someone around.

515
35:35.947 --> 35:37.198
Get out.

516
35:38.241 --> 35:39.992
I told you to get out.

517
35:40.076 --> 35:41.953
Go keep a lookout or something!

518
35:42.578 --> 35:44.997
Are you doing something that needs a lookout?

519
35:59.887 --> 36:02.181
I could've finished charging by now. Get out now.

520
36:02.265 --> 36:03.599
You're not leaving?

521
36:04.350 --> 36:05.309
Get out already.

522
36:09.397 --> 36:10.773
Get out!

523
36:21.033 --> 36:22.868
TS HOTEL VICE PRESIDENT YOON DONG-SEOK

524
36:30.126 --> 36:30.960
Yes.

525
36:33.504 --> 36:34.505
It's me.

526
36:42.638 --> 36:44.515
He just won't listen.

527
36:49.937 --> 36:51.981
Shall we… do it now?

528
36:54.191 --> 36:55.026
I guess.

529
36:55.109 --> 36:56.193
Well…

530
36:57.945 --> 36:58.779
Here.

531
37:12.043 --> 37:13.419
Oh, it's over 50%.

532
37:13.502 --> 37:15.796
It's half full. That's in the safe range, isn't it?

533
37:17.048 --> 37:17.882
Actually…

534
37:21.135 --> 37:22.345
Ms. Na Bo-bae?

535
37:23.346 --> 37:24.347
Yes?

536
37:24.930 --> 37:25.765
I was

537
37:26.265 --> 37:29.101
just talking about holding hands.

538
37:33.022 --> 37:35.024
What? Oh gosh.

539
37:37.485 --> 37:38.778
I thought…

540
37:38.861 --> 37:42.615
You opened your arms wide like this, so I thought you wanted a hug.

541
37:42.698 --> 37:43.616
That's why I…

542
37:43.699 --> 37:46.577
Man, this is more than enough.

543
37:46.660 --> 37:48.245
-Thank you. -Sure.

544
37:48.329 --> 37:49.330
Yeah.

545
37:50.581 --> 37:51.832
Then I'll…

546
37:52.458 --> 37:53.709
Who was it?

547
37:53.793 --> 37:57.004
Oh, the director. I'll go over the script one last time with him.

548
37:57.088 --> 37:58.172
Okay.

549
37:59.882 --> 38:01.175
-I'll get going. -See you.

550
38:04.261 --> 38:05.763
Thank you.

551
38:05.846 --> 38:07.723
Oh. Sure.

552
38:26.242 --> 38:28.077
-The butterfly… -Stop asking me.

553
38:28.160 --> 38:29.328
Sorry I'm late.

554
38:29.412 --> 38:31.080
Go to the set already!

555
38:31.163 --> 38:33.290
-We'll go without the butterfly. -Ms. Na.

556
38:33.374 --> 38:34.667
How do we express this?

557
38:34.750 --> 38:36.127
Where? Oh, here.

558
38:36.836 --> 38:38.712
-Is it done? -Looks like an early wrap.

559
38:38.796 --> 38:40.673
-Can I see the script? -Here.

560
38:46.470 --> 38:48.973
Ms. Na, I have a question.

561
38:49.974 --> 38:50.808
Yeah.

562
38:50.891 --> 38:52.560
-The emotion here… -Which part?

563
38:52.643 --> 38:54.353
I just wanted an excuse to talk.

564
38:55.354 --> 38:56.605
The script's great.

565
38:56.689 --> 38:58.107
Oh, come on.

566
38:58.649 --> 39:01.735
It's only one minute long, but your hard work shows.

567
39:01.819 --> 39:05.114
It's in script format, but it's my first commercial.

568
39:05.197 --> 39:06.115
Is it okay?

569
39:07.533 --> 39:09.243
What's with those two?

570
39:09.952 --> 39:11.662
So you noticed it too.

571
39:11.745 --> 39:12.580
Yeah.

572
39:12.663 --> 39:16.333
Do you think something's going on between those two?

573
39:17.376 --> 39:20.337
I thought Ms. Na and Mr. Baek were a sure thing,

574
39:20.421 --> 39:22.214
but maybe it's those two instead.

575
39:22.298 --> 39:24.800
Come on. Watch what you say.

576
39:25.301 --> 39:26.719
You said it too, Ms. Go.

577
39:26.802 --> 39:27.761
Well…

578
39:28.262 --> 39:31.974
I mean, they look good together.

579
39:39.940 --> 39:42.651
Look good together? Give me a break.

580
39:56.457 --> 39:58.584
Shouldn't he go deeper?

581
39:58.667 --> 39:59.793
Looks good to me.

582
39:59.877 --> 40:01.795
Besides, it's really shallow here.

583
40:01.879 --> 40:03.005
No.

584
40:03.631 --> 40:07.468
I think he should dive from here to here and do a few laps

585
40:07.551 --> 40:09.553
to make it look real.

586
40:09.637 --> 40:10.971
Is that really necessary?

587
40:11.847 --> 40:14.850
Aren't you a professional? Isn't directing all about the visuals?

588
40:14.934 --> 40:18.979
He should dive, swim around, and spin like a dolphin

589
40:19.063 --> 40:24.485
so we can really show off how big the pool is at TS Resort Jeju.

590
40:24.568 --> 40:25.945
Not even pro swimmers would do that.

591
40:26.028 --> 40:27.279
Excuse me?

592
40:27.363 --> 40:29.323
Okay, fine.

593
40:29.406 --> 40:30.574
Cut.

594
40:31.075 --> 40:33.494
Sorry, but let's shoot that again.

595
40:33.577 --> 40:35.621
Eun-ho, sorry, but after a short break,

596
40:35.704 --> 40:39.083
could you swim butterfly like a dolphin from here to there?

597
40:39.166 --> 40:40.084
Sure.

598
40:43.045 --> 40:45.381
Tell him to do three laps.

599
40:45.881 --> 40:47.675
We may have to do it a few times.

600
40:47.758 --> 40:48.676
Sure.

601
40:48.759 --> 40:49.802
Sorry. Thank you.

602
40:50.302 --> 40:51.595
Happy now?

603
40:53.347 --> 40:55.432
-Ms. Na. -Yes.

604
40:57.184 --> 40:58.227
Well…

605
40:58.310 --> 40:59.520
How did I do?

606
41:00.145 --> 41:01.480
I should've worked out more.

607
41:04.275 --> 41:06.819
No. You already look great.

608
41:11.073 --> 41:14.577
Did she just give Ji Eun-ho's abs a thumbs-up?

609
41:17.037 --> 41:19.456
I'm nervous because you're watching me.

610
41:19.540 --> 41:21.041
I might be shaking a little.

611
41:21.667 --> 41:24.545
I told you not to go around flirting without thinking.

612
41:24.628 --> 41:27.047
What do you mean, without thinking? I mean it.

613
41:33.971 --> 41:36.181
See? People get the wrong idea.

614
41:36.265 --> 41:38.392
No. They won't.

615
41:39.143 --> 41:40.936
-Aren't you cold? -I'm fine.

616
41:43.272 --> 41:44.898
Do you want some water?

617
41:45.941 --> 41:46.775
What's…

618
41:49.278 --> 41:50.613
Go take a break.

619
41:51.238 --> 41:52.281
What's with him?

620
42:02.124 --> 42:04.376
-We'll start with the dolphin! -Yeah.

621
42:04.460 --> 42:05.336
Eun-ho, you okay?

622
42:05.419 --> 42:06.795
-Let's go! -I think it's great.

623
42:06.879 --> 42:09.006
-I love it. -I know.

624
42:09.923 --> 42:10.883
Thanks.

625
42:22.728 --> 42:25.314
Eun-ho! Why are you at the grill?

626
42:25.397 --> 42:26.649
-Come here. -It's done.

627
42:26.732 --> 42:28.734
Let's sit down and eat. Come on, everyone.

628
42:28.817 --> 42:29.902
Come on. Let's eat.

629
42:29.985 --> 42:31.528
-Fill your glasses. -Fill them.

630
42:31.612 --> 42:33.572
-We should drink together. -Fill them.

631
42:33.656 --> 42:34.490
Come here.

632
42:34.573 --> 42:36.116
You're too loud.

633
42:36.200 --> 42:38.452
-Thank you. -Don't mention it.

634
42:38.535 --> 42:40.079
-Fill your glasses. -Fill them.

635
42:40.162 --> 42:41.497
-Glasses up. -Up!

636
42:41.580 --> 42:43.999
All right. Glasses up!

637
42:44.083 --> 42:45.668
Here's to Yeom Min-kyu!

638
42:45.751 --> 42:47.044
Cheers!

639
42:47.127 --> 42:49.296
-Cheers. -Cheers.

640
42:50.506 --> 42:51.632
Thank you.

641
42:58.180 --> 43:00.808
Mr. Ji, you worked so hard today.

642
43:00.891 --> 43:03.477
Not at all. Everyone else worked harder.

643
43:03.560 --> 43:05.771
Mr. Ji, eat up.

644
43:05.854 --> 43:07.231
Thank you.

645
43:07.314 --> 43:09.566
You don't have to do this. I can help myself.

646
43:13.654 --> 43:14.488
Ms. Na.

647
43:14.571 --> 43:16.699
You should take off your gloves and dig in.

648
43:22.830 --> 43:25.541
Wow, you two must be really close.

649
43:25.624 --> 43:26.917
I hear you go way back.

650
43:27.000 --> 43:30.045
Yeah. Those two are tight!

651
43:30.129 --> 43:32.256
Yes, we are pretty tight.

652
43:33.132 --> 43:35.134
She means the world to me.

653
43:49.148 --> 43:50.607
He can be kind of confusing.

654
43:50.691 --> 43:53.152
He's dangerously charming.

655
43:53.235 --> 43:55.237
Always making people get the wrong idea.

656
43:55.988 --> 43:57.573
Weird way to say you're a fan.

657
43:58.157 --> 44:00.492
So you aren't actually dating?

658
44:00.576 --> 44:01.827
You two look great together.

659
44:02.619 --> 44:03.579
Really?

660
44:04.580 --> 44:06.415
Ms. Na, she says we look great together.

661
44:07.666 --> 44:09.835
How could I date Eun-ho?

662
44:09.918 --> 44:14.423
Is Ms. Na going to make the entertainment headlines

663
44:14.506 --> 44:16.800
before her miniseries even debuts?

664
44:16.884 --> 44:18.969
As "Ji Eun-ho's girl."

665
44:19.052 --> 44:20.137
Eun-ho's girl!

666
44:22.598 --> 44:24.057
That's enough. You're drunk.

667
44:28.687 --> 44:31.523
I can't listen to this anymore. I'm getting uncomfortable.

668
44:32.024 --> 44:33.650
This is the problem with our society.

669
44:34.443 --> 44:38.030
When we see a man and a woman who are close or around the same age,

670
44:38.113 --> 44:41.742
we always try to set them up and push them to date.

671
44:42.534 --> 44:46.830
It's nothing more than entertainment for thoughtless bystanders!

672
44:50.542 --> 44:53.086
Isn't it about time we stopped this?

673
44:53.712 --> 44:55.380
Just a fan!

674
44:56.924 --> 44:57.966
That's what she said.

675
44:58.717 --> 45:00.177
Mutual fans!

676
45:00.761 --> 45:01.678
Nothing more.

677
45:06.308 --> 45:08.185
Show some restraint.

678
45:08.268 --> 45:10.062
What's your problem?

679
45:10.938 --> 45:12.773
Did I do something wrong?

680
45:14.691 --> 45:16.693
Stop eating garlic, sir.

681
45:18.237 --> 45:19.404
What's with him?

682
45:23.283 --> 45:24.827
Did I do something wrong?

683
45:24.910 --> 45:28.080
People get on edge before something big.

684
45:28.163 --> 45:29.456
Something big?

685
45:29.957 --> 45:30.999
Is something going on?

686
45:32.918 --> 45:34.127
Oh.

687
45:34.628 --> 45:37.965
Actually, the chairwoman's been pushing us to get married,

688
45:39.675 --> 45:41.718
so I think we'll be setting a date soon.

689
45:45.764 --> 45:48.809
You two are actually getting married?

690
45:48.892 --> 45:49.977
Ho-rang.

691
45:50.477 --> 45:51.645
Is it true?

692
45:52.396 --> 45:55.190
Why is everyone so surprised? It already made the news.

693
45:56.483 --> 45:59.570
It's almost like you thought we weren't going to get married.

694
45:59.653 --> 46:01.029
No. Not at all.

695
46:01.113 --> 46:04.491
My sincere congratulations. Invite me to the wedding, okay?

696
46:04.575 --> 46:05.534
A get-together!

697
46:05.617 --> 46:07.995
-Ho-rang. A get-together! -It's not happening--

698
46:11.790 --> 46:13.959
You said you needed three months.

699
46:14.585 --> 46:16.670
The three months aren't up yet.

700
46:19.131 --> 46:20.632
The chairwoman's backed off, hasn't she?

701
46:22.593 --> 46:25.345
I asked her to be patient a little longer.

702
46:28.473 --> 46:30.434
You should stay on my good side.

703
46:57.794 --> 47:00.505
Bo-bae, want to get some fresh air?

704
47:13.769 --> 47:15.062
We'll be right back.

705
47:21.735 --> 47:23.570
Bo-bae, are you okay?

706
47:23.654 --> 47:24.488
Yeah.

707
47:28.492 --> 47:29.326
Huh?

708
47:30.285 --> 47:32.120
My shoelace is untied.

709
47:32.204 --> 47:33.580
Bo-bae. Hold on.

710
47:35.749 --> 47:36.708
Sit here.

711
47:42.381 --> 47:44.800
You can't just touch me like that.

712
47:45.634 --> 47:48.178
I know. I'll tie it without touching you.

713
47:48.261 --> 47:51.890
What do you know? You might actually…

714
47:52.391 --> 47:55.268
I really do know, Bo-bae. I know your condition.

715
47:56.937 --> 47:59.314
We've known each other for three years.

716
47:59.815 --> 48:01.024
How could I not know?

717
48:01.108 --> 48:03.485
If you knew, why did you…

718
48:05.529 --> 48:07.823
It seemed like you wanted to hide it.

719
48:11.827 --> 48:14.496
I didn't want someone I like to know I knew their weakness.

720
48:20.585 --> 48:21.628
And

721
48:22.629 --> 48:25.966
I also know nothing happens when you touch Mr. Baek.

722
48:28.677 --> 48:30.262
He's…

723
48:30.345 --> 48:32.305
I don't know why it doesn't affect him…

724
48:39.730 --> 48:40.981
but it doesn't matter now.

725
48:43.442 --> 48:44.317
Bo-bae.

726
48:48.280 --> 48:50.282
To you, am I really

727
48:51.450 --> 48:53.535
just a close friend

728
48:54.745 --> 48:56.121
and a good actor?

729
48:58.165 --> 48:59.291
That's it?

730
49:02.544 --> 49:03.378
Eun-ho.

731
49:03.462 --> 49:04.671
That's not how I feel.

732
49:05.630 --> 49:06.465
MBS DRAMA

733
49:06.548 --> 49:08.508
CEHONGDAM INTERNATIONAL UNIVERSITY AUDITION

734
49:18.268 --> 49:21.146
"I just didn't know how to comfort you, so…"

735
49:21.229 --> 49:23.857
"Earlier, I tried to comfort you, but I just…"

736
49:23.940 --> 49:27.069
"Earlier, I tried to comfort you, but I only made you uncomfortable."

737
49:29.154 --> 49:30.697
"I just didn't know how to…"

738
49:30.781 --> 49:32.365
"They say…"

739
49:32.449 --> 49:33.492
"Earlier…"

740
49:34.117 --> 49:36.703
"…the darkest hour is just before dawn."

741
49:37.204 --> 49:41.124
"They say the darkest hour is just before dawn."

742
49:41.708 --> 49:43.418
"There's a saying…"

743
49:46.213 --> 49:47.214
Dark…

744
49:50.217 --> 49:52.260
"Don't give up…"

745
49:54.387 --> 49:55.764
BLACK PARTNER AUDITION

746
50:24.751 --> 50:27.295
-Hello! -Oh, the male lead is here.

747
50:27.379 --> 50:29.256
Everyone, let's give him a big hand!

748
50:39.182 --> 50:40.016
He's so handsome!

749
50:41.017 --> 50:43.728
Eun-ho, meet our writer.

750
50:48.275 --> 50:50.944
-Hello, Ms. Writer. -Hello.

751
50:51.570 --> 50:52.779
So you're the writer.

752
50:57.659 --> 50:58.910
You are the one

753
50:59.619 --> 51:01.538
who makes my heart race.

754
51:06.877 --> 51:09.254
Can't you see me that way too?

755
51:11.756 --> 51:12.591
That's…

756
51:13.175 --> 51:16.720
Hey, everyone's heart races.

757
51:17.220 --> 51:19.806
And let's say I return your feelings.

758
51:19.890 --> 51:24.352
You might never be able to hold my hand or kiss me for the rest of your life.

759
51:24.436 --> 51:25.687
You'd be okay with that?

760
51:26.646 --> 51:28.773
I waited three years for the right moment.

761
51:29.274 --> 51:31.610
"When I'm a better actor."

762
51:31.693 --> 51:33.153
"When I'm more successful."

763
51:35.780 --> 51:38.575
But I realized there's no perfect time.

764
51:39.910 --> 51:40.869
Eun-ho.

765
51:45.207 --> 51:46.249
I like you.

766
51:50.337 --> 51:51.880
Can't this be enough?

767
52:36.341 --> 52:39.302
It's obvious this is an important moment. Let's not interrupt.

768
52:41.179 --> 52:42.472
Let go.

769
52:45.392 --> 52:46.726
Do you like Ms. Na Bo-bae?

770
52:52.065 --> 52:56.236
I don't see why I should answer that.

771
52:56.319 --> 52:58.029
You really don't?

772
52:58.113 --> 53:00.156
Are you threatening me?

773
53:01.116 --> 53:02.867
No, I'm just telling the truth.

774
53:03.618 --> 53:05.787
Whether we get married or not,

775
53:05.870 --> 53:08.206
I'm the one cutting you some slack for the next three months.

776
53:08.290 --> 53:10.834
I asked for time to prove myself,

777
53:10.917 --> 53:13.044
not for you to push me around.

778
53:14.296 --> 53:15.255
Also…

779
53:20.343 --> 53:21.928
you asked me if I liked her.

780
53:23.763 --> 53:26.141
If I said I like her,

781
53:26.850 --> 53:28.310
would you call off the wedding?

782
53:32.063 --> 53:35.608
In all my plans from A to Z,

783
53:35.692 --> 53:39.654
there isn't a single outcome where I don't take over TS.

784
53:40.697 --> 53:44.534
I'll put TS back on top of the industry, no matter what.

785
53:44.617 --> 53:46.786
But if you think about it,

786
53:46.870 --> 53:51.333
the fact that you have so many plans means you're not certain.

787
53:52.709 --> 53:54.377
Anyway, I'll wait for you.

788
53:54.461 --> 53:57.339
I'm curious to see what you're capable of, Mr. Baek.

789
54:22.655 --> 54:23.823
Mr. Baek Ho-rang.

790
54:27.911 --> 54:30.622
Where have you been all this time?

791
54:31.998 --> 54:36.127
I just went for a walk to sober up.

792
54:37.295 --> 54:39.422
What are you doing here?

793
54:39.923 --> 54:44.427
Earlier, after announcing your wedding, you were whispering with Ms. Han.

794
54:50.308 --> 54:51.142
Well…

795
54:52.477 --> 54:53.728
Does it bother you?

796
54:55.980 --> 54:57.273
No.

797
55:05.990 --> 55:06.950
"Still,

798
55:07.617 --> 55:09.160
let's keep going."

799
55:11.871 --> 55:13.748
Where did that come from?

800
55:17.377 --> 55:22.465
"Even if the whole world feels like an enemy and a burden,

801
55:23.925 --> 55:26.386
and nothing works no matter how hard you try,

802
55:26.469 --> 55:28.346
try again."

803
55:29.389 --> 55:32.475
"Even through tears, don't give up."

804
55:33.393 --> 55:34.394
"For now…

805
55:36.396 --> 55:37.397
let's just…

806
55:40.483 --> 55:42.402
keep going."

807
55:47.949 --> 55:50.326
You watched Wistful Youth?

808
55:53.705 --> 55:55.707
You kept talking about it, so…

809
55:57.500 --> 55:58.668
To you,

810
55:58.751 --> 56:03.298
it may be just another one-hour drama no one knows about,

811
56:03.381 --> 56:07.093
but it means the world to me.

812
56:08.386 --> 56:09.512
Still,

813
56:11.347 --> 56:12.974
let's keep going.

814
56:13.683 --> 56:16.227
Even if the whole world feels like an enemy and a burden,

815
56:16.728 --> 56:19.898
and nothing works no matter how hard you try,

816
56:19.981 --> 56:21.232
try again.

817
56:22.567 --> 56:24.360
Even through tears, don't give up.

818
56:26.112 --> 56:29.491
For now, let's just keep going.

819
56:53.556 --> 56:58.394
Well, I can see why you and Mr. Ji Eun-ho have such a special relationship.

820
56:58.478 --> 57:01.731
If I acted in a script like that,

821
57:02.440 --> 57:04.692
I'd become a fan of the writer too.

822
57:10.865 --> 57:11.824
You know,

823
57:12.909 --> 57:13.868
I'm also…

824
57:20.375 --> 57:21.501
a fan of yours…

825
57:23.503 --> 57:24.796
Ms. Na.

826
57:27.382 --> 57:28.675
There you go again.

827
57:29.467 --> 57:31.928
It's okay. No need to say nice things.

828
57:32.011 --> 57:33.263
I want to…

829
57:35.473 --> 57:36.474
keep going

830
57:38.268 --> 57:39.769
with you.

831
57:41.980 --> 57:42.981
For now,

832
57:44.065 --> 57:45.108
let's just

833
57:46.192 --> 57:47.277
keep going.

834
57:51.281 --> 57:52.323
Wherever it takes us.

835
58:01.749 --> 58:02.834
It's me.

836
58:04.335 --> 58:05.962
Did you get a good shot earlier?

837
58:10.091 --> 58:14.012
Edit the video to get Ji Eun-ho's fans riled up.

838
58:15.096 --> 58:16.848
Make it really trashy…

839
58:19.100 --> 58:20.310
and entertaining.

840
58:21.769 --> 58:23.980
Is this for real? My gosh.

841
58:24.063 --> 58:26.107
-Crazy, right? -This is insane.

842
58:26.733 --> 58:29.235
-Good morning. Did you all sleep well? -My gosh.

843
58:32.947 --> 58:36.034
Impressive. Truly impressive.

844
58:36.701 --> 58:40.288
I told you. I saw her doing it with Mr. Baek too.

845
58:41.414 --> 58:43.041
How did she even get to Eun-ho?

846
58:50.214 --> 58:51.341
Yes, Ms. Chu.

847
58:55.637 --> 58:56.471
Sorry?

848
58:57.096 --> 59:00.224
The shocking identity of the woman Ji Eun-ho proposed to.

849
59:00.308 --> 59:04.270
A video of Ji Eun-ho proposing was leaked, sending all of Korea into a frenzy.

850
59:04.354 --> 59:07.774
It turns out the woman in the video is a drama writer.

851
59:07.857 --> 59:10.735
She wrote the one-ep drama that gave Ji Eun-ho his first lead role,

852
59:10.818 --> 59:12.362
then dropped off the radar.

853
59:12.445 --> 59:15.323
There's been a lot of buzz about her new drama,

854
59:15.406 --> 59:17.867
but turns out she got it by flirting with Ji Eun-ho.

855
59:18.451 --> 59:21.120
A real drama writer should let her script do the talking.

856
59:23.289 --> 59:25.124
SHE WROTE JI EUN-HO'S FIRST LEAD DRAMA

857
59:25.208 --> 59:26.876
TRYING TO BAG A CELEB AND LEVEL UP

858
59:26.959 --> 59:28.211
Man, this is…

859
59:28.294 --> 59:30.046
Damn.

860
59:30.129 --> 59:31.589
It's only been up for a bit,

861
59:31.673 --> 59:34.509
but there are already many videos with the same comments.

862
59:35.593 --> 59:37.804
This isn't one person. It's coordinated.

863
59:39.263 --> 59:41.891
I'll get all the details as fast as I can.

864
59:41.974 --> 59:43.601
We should get back to Seoul.

865
59:43.685 --> 59:46.813
If fans swarm the airport, it'll be a nightmare.

866
59:46.896 --> 59:49.399
We should all head to the airport separately.

867
01:00:20.346 --> 01:00:21.889
This isn't good.

868
01:00:22.724 --> 01:00:24.767
We probably shouldn't move as a group.

869
01:00:24.851 --> 01:00:25.893
We should split up.

870
01:00:25.977 --> 01:00:27.770
-Seo-jeong, bring the luggage. -Sorry?

871
01:00:28.354 --> 01:00:30.314
Grab the luggage. Follow me!

872
01:00:31.649 --> 01:00:32.483
Seo-jeong!

873
01:00:32.567 --> 01:00:33.568
Hide well. Okay?

874
01:00:50.668 --> 01:00:51.753
Isn't she that writer?

875
01:00:51.836 --> 01:00:53.337
-Let me see. -What?

876
01:00:53.421 --> 01:00:54.505
It's her.

877
01:00:54.589 --> 01:00:55.423
It's that woman!

878
01:00:55.506 --> 01:00:57.467
-Follow me. -Damn, she's all covered up.

879
01:00:57.550 --> 01:00:59.844
-It's her. -It's that woman.

880
01:01:06.559 --> 01:01:08.436
-It's her. -It's that woman.

881
01:01:08.519 --> 01:01:10.229
Damn, she's all covered up.

882
01:01:10.313 --> 01:01:13.024
-Leave our Eun-ho alone! -You crazy bitch!

883
01:01:27.205 --> 01:01:28.790
I need to hold it in.

884
01:01:30.208 --> 01:01:31.501
I have to hold it in.

885
01:01:32.794 --> 01:01:34.504
No, Na Bo-bae.

886
01:01:34.587 --> 01:01:36.839
Hold it in. If you can't hold it in here…

887
01:04:53.786 --> 01:04:58.416
Subtitle translation by: Sung In Jang
